facts=[dict(id='f-match',meaning='Tracker records the greatest reported replicated log index for each presently included voter.',identity={'tracker':'leader-term commitment instance','participant':'ServerID'},validity_context='Only voter IDs in this tracker configuration; reported persistence is inferred from local store completion or successful peer response.',representation=['commitment.matchIndexes'],durability='Volatile tracker; underlying peer logs are separately persisted.',recovery='Recreated with zero match indices on each leader term.',source_ids=['s-commit','s-dispatch','s-match']),dict(id='f-committed',meaning='Raft records a commit-index prefix for processing; this alone does not say that the FSM has applied it.',identity={'node':'Raft instance','prefix':'commit index'},validity_context='Leader majority calculation or follower accepted leader commit propagation in its term/log context.',representation=['raftState.commitIndex'],durability='Volatile index; log and snapshot retain history.',recovery='Startup restores snapshot applied position; subsequent consensus propagates commit knowledge.',source_ids=['s-commit','s-leader-loop','s-append','s-start']),dict(id='f-verify-count',meaning='Verification future has counted self and affirmative replication notifications up to its voter-derived numeric threshold.',identity={'operation':'verifyFuture pointer'},validity_context='One future registered while leader; counted notifications do not themselves retain peer suffrage or term.',representation=['verifyFuture.votes','verifyFuture.quorumSize','verifyFuture.notifyCh'],durability='Volatile only.',recovery='No recovery; leader exit fails pending tracked futures.',source_ids=['s-verify','s-notify','s-verify-vote','s-leader-loop'])]
formation='Leader assigns term/index, stores locally and replicates to all configured peers. Successful append or snapshot responses report match indices to the leader-term tracker. Only configured voters contribute to its majority, and the majority index must reach the first current-term entry. The main loop consumes commit notifications, updates committed configuration and queues the committed prefix. Followers validate previous log context, repair conflicting suffixes, accept leader commit propagation and queue their prefix. runFSM serializes actual application and responds to local futures afterward; queue position alone is not completion.'
context='Follower timeout can start a voter election. Optional pre-vote precedes durable term increment and persisted self vote. Requests are scoped to one election reply channel; recipient eligibility, freshness, leader and prior-vote checks constrain grants. Majority establishes leadership. Higher terms, failed voter lease, replication stale-term signal or committed local removal end authority. Leader exit stops workers and fails pending work; new leadership creates a fresh commitment object and no-op. Transfer catches up a selected peer then sends TimeoutNow; it bypasses pre-vote and temporarily prevents new leader client work.'
connection='Election log freshness preserves prior eligible history, while committing a new-term no-op establishes the new leader commitment boundary. Old election reply channels and old replication commitment objects remain separate from new attempts/terms. Latest logged configuration controls election and quorum membership before its commitment, but a further configuration requires prior configuration and current-term entry commitment. Conflicting follower suffix removal restores committed membership; snapshots restore configuration and applied prefix before suffix scanning or resumed participation. Already queued committed work remains FSM work across role change, while uncommitted leader futures become uncertain errors. VerifyLeader is a separate authority consumer using replication notifications; its voter-derived threshold and all-peer registration require eligibility investigation.'
path=lambda e,bs,ss:dict(explanation=e,behavior_ids=bs,source_ids=ss)
